Package: gnome-tray-overflow
Version: @VERSION@
Section: gnome
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: gnome-shell (>= 45)
Recommends: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Maintainer: Pedro Schneider <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/correaschneider/gnome-tray-overflow
Description: GNOME Shell extension: tray overflow for AppIndicator icons
 Hides unpinned system tray (AppIndicator) icons behind a ⋯ button in the
 top bar, like the Windows tray overflow. Left click opens a drawer with the
 hidden icons; right click lists every icon with a switch to pin it.
